tool_args.old_string:
We present a factorial diagnostic of temporal abstraction in DreamerV3, identifying trained $\dt$-embedding with multi-rate data exposure as the causal factor behind CIVO ($\nve \geq 1.5\times$, 27/29, AUROC${=}0.971$). The RSSM's $2.78\times$ reward prediction gap drives critic overestimation through forward-pass mechanisms that no gradient-level intervention eliminates (SGS 0/3--1/6). In pure-imagination training, dual critics converge to identical functions ($\rho > 0.999$), rendering Double Q pessimism ineffective; min $+$ capacity achieves 3/4 prevention on Walker but not cross-environment. The feedback architecture---MPC re-planning versus imagination-based bootstrapping---is the structural factor.

\paragraph{Limitations and future work.}
Our analysis centers on Walker Walk with fewer cross-environment seeds using proprioceptive state; generalization to pixel observations and transformer-based world models remains open. The NVE threshold is validated in-sample ($n{=}29$); held-out evaluation is needed. Hierarchical approaches \citep{hafner2022director, gumbsch2024thick} that avoid flat $\dt$-conditioning are a promising direction. Code and logs: upon acceptance.

